{
  "name": "rope_bridge_72",
  "version": 2,
  "introduced_by": "jadewater",
  "notes": "The Order's lacquered rope bridge, 72 m along local X and 3 m wide, a 2 m plank deck with gaps between the boards sagging 1.75 m at mid-span, two main cables, hand ropes 1.1 m up on hangers every 2 m, and a red gate 2.25 m clear at each end. Base rim: place at the gap's middle between two towers whose tops are the same height (mesa `top`), bearing 0 for east-west, 90 for north-south; each end should rest 3-6 m onto a tower.",
